ld make us sick or kill us and  yet we don't get up in the morning  worried about it because this miracle  system detects those threats assesses  them as dangerous or not  responds to them destroys the ones that  must and learns from it sort of the  principle of vaccination  only when our immune system is weakened  are we suddenly vulnerable to things  well we have risk immune systems in our  organizations and i would argue in our  wider society and when that risk immune  system is weakened or doesn't function  well suddenly things which really  shouldn't cause us huge problems covet  19 for example is not an amazingly 10  feet tall unbeatable virus right  we knew what to do about it we knew it  was coming and we got this miracle  vaccine at record speed and yet still  we struggle we struggle because our risk  immune system  is weakened yeah and that risk immune  system we  we define 10 factors  risk control factors communication  narrative diversity bias timing action  number of those and all of those operate  as a system and if we keep that healthy  and we can do that we have agency over  that  so risk is not always something terrible  to us it's also an opportunity to be  more resilient and it's about how we  handle it you say you chose a soldier's  life because you like taking risk what  does that say about you  well when i was young i looked at people  who were timid  and i decided i didn't want to be that  and so i wouldn't be timid i went into a  a line of business where i thought  i would be taught and forced to take on  risk and also to be honest you like the  idea of being viewed as someone who's a  risk taker be viewed as the bold of  course and it becomes self-reinforcing  it's a great book and apple application  that that we can use on many areas of  our life thank you so much general  stanley mcchrystal risk a user's guide  on sale right now very kind

